# BUGS

Only power domains' and clocks' on and off, and clocks' rates, are sent: no performance levels, sensors, resets or the platform's own messages (the second mailbox and its notifications aren't read).
The channels are polled, not interrupted.
A CPPC register is written only where it is in a range this agent holds: registers in another page that no driver owns aren't reachable through it.
Firmware's SMC channel exists only by a board rule; nothing in ACPI describes it.
